Package: rcisignal
Title: Quality Checks for Reverse-Correlation Data and Classification Images
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R:
    person("Manuel", "Oliveira",
           email   = "m.j.barbosa.de.oliveira@tue.nl",
           role    = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6220-0695"))
Description: A consolidated toolkit for assessing the quality of reverse
    correlation (RC) experiments end-to-end. Input-side diagnostics
    catch silent data-processing errors before classification image (CI)
    computation: response coding, response time, response bias, trial
    counts, duplicate trials, stimulus-pool alignment, and 'rcicr'
    version compatibility. Output-side analyses quantify CI quality
    after computation: within-condition reliability via permuted
    split-half with Spearman-Brown correction and ICC(3,k); between-
    condition discriminability via Welch pixel-wise t-tests, cluster-
    based permutation with family-wise error control (Maris &
    Oostenveld, 2007) and threshold-free cluster enhancement (Smith &
    Nichols, 2009); per-producer informational value with a trial-
    count-matched reference distribution that closes a calibration gap
    in the original 'rcicr' implementation. Supports the standard
    two-image forced-choice (2IFC) pipeline via 'rcicr' (Dotsch, 2016,
    2023) and the Brief-RC pipeline (Schmitz, Rougier, & Yzerbyt,
    2024) implemented natively. Operates directly on the pixel-level
    signal produced by the original producers, so it does not depend
    on a second-phase trait-rating study.
